WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:00.600
Alex.

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.101
Just moments

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:01.434
ago, we

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.036
learned of two more attacks,

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.871
rocket attacks and a drone attack

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.439
against facilities housing U.S.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.407
troops in Syria.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.174
That played out

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.509
just over the course of the last

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.143
few hours.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:10.477
First,

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.178
a number of rockets were fired

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.247
at the Conoco oil fields in central

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.181
or eastern Syria.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.816
Again, a facility that houses U.S.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:17.417
troops.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.918
That, according to a US official

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.153
in that attack.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:20.754
One U.S.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.155
service members was injured

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.923
but is in stable condition.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.393
Just a short time after that 31 way

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.395
uvs or suicide drones

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.863
attacked another facility

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.965
not too far away known as Green Village,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.400
also housing U.S. troops.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.467
According to the official,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.269
two of those three drones were shot down.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.571
The other did not injure U.S.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.873
troops based at that facility

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.174
or do damage to infrastructure.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.375
But this all happened

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.176
very quickly

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.411
just within the course of the last

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.979
36 or 48 hours.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:46.379
These are

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.581
this is now for attacks within Syria

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.682
against bases

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.684
and facilities, housing U.S. troops.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.886
The question, of course, now

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:53.820
how does the US

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.722
how does the Biden administration respond

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.090
to what is quickly escalating

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.861
a late night strike in northeast Syria.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:02.695
Ambulances

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.130
rushing to the scene as fire

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.698
burns in the distance.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.032
U.S.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.100
striking what officials say

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.968
were ammunition depots and intelligence

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:09.936
sites used by

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.271
militias linked to Iran's

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:14.074
Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:14.574
The U.S.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.408
called the strike

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.477
carried out by two F-15 fighters.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.846
A proportionate and deliberate action

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.281
after a one way drone attack

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.682
killed an American contractor

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.751
earlier Thursday near Hasaka in Syria.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:25.785
Five U.S.

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.553
service members

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.720
and another contractor

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.289
were wounded in the attack

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.057
Early Friday morning, another U.S.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.559
base in Syria coming under attack

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.527
from a barrage of ten rockets.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.062
The Pentagon said the U.S.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.864
placing the blame on Iran.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.200
Iran certainly again backs these groups

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.668
and by default,

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.169
therefore has a responsibility

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.105
to ensure that they're not contributing

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.339
to insecurity and stability.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.541
But clearly, they continue to do that.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.977
Syria has become a crossroads of conflict

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:51.945
in the Middle East.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.413
Iranian proxies have carried out

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.215
rocket and drone attacks against U.S.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.916
forces, and Russia has begun

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.018
flying armed fighters over U.S.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.553
positions in the country.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.254
For the U.S.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.122
and its footprint

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.057
of about 900 troops in Syria,

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.959
the focus remains ISIS.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.594
We don't seek a war with Iran.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.194
We're not

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.863
looking for an armed conflict

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.597
with that country

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.765
or another war in the region.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.800
We do

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.802
seek to protect our mission in Syria,

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.604
which is about defeating ISIS.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.139
On Thursday, the commander of U.S.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:20.340
Central Command, General

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.508
Eric Parrilla, told

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.709
the House Armed Services

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:23.543
Committee hearing

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:24.878
that Iran and its proxies

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.479
have fired drones or rockets.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.047
78 times U.S.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.483
forces since the beginning of 20, 21,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.986
nearly one attack every ten days.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.621
So what Iran does to hide its hand

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.055
is they use Iranian proxies.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.624
That's that's either UAV

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.025
or or rockets

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.527
to be able to attack our forces in either

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.395
Iraq or Syria.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.632
Are these considered acts of war by Iran?

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.133
They are

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:47.967
being done by the

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.502
Iranian proxies, is what I would tell

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.336
you, Congressman.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:50.803
The U.S.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:51.838
has carried out attacks

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.106
against Iranian proxies

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:53.573
in Syria

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.774
before targeting

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.242
either enemy infrastructure

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.310
or launch vehicles.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.912
Used to attack U.S.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.046
forces.

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:01.347
So just to review

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.849
where the situation stands right now,

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:03.950
within the last couple of hours,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.051
we have seen, again,

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.253
two more attacks on facilities in Syria.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.521
Housing U.S. troops.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.489
A number of rockets

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.491
launched at the Conoco oil fields

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.559
where there are troops

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:13.693
based there, according to a U.S.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.460
official familiar

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.229
with the intelligence about the attack.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.664
One service member was injured

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.399
but is in stable condition.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.600
And then there were 31

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.100
where you have

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.368
these are suicide drones

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:22.936
that were launched

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.137
against another facility

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.004
known as Green Village

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.306
that also houses U.S.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:26.906
troops

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.408
Two of those drones were intercepted.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.643
A third damaged a facility there,

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.412
but did no injury to U.S.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.580
troops who are stationed there.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.814
The question now, Alex,

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.683
how does the Biden administration respond

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.050
to this?

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.251
General Eric Guerrilla,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.085
the commander of U.S.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.386
Central Command, made it clear that

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.555
if Iranian proxies continued to attack,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:42.989
the U.S.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.623
would very much

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:44.924
reserve the right to respond

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.826
and has options to do so.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:47.894
Let's bring in CNN chief

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.529
White House correspondent Phil Mattingly.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.897
He is traveling with the president

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.631
in Canada.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.599
Also joining us,

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.800
CNN military analyst

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.668
and retired Air Force Colonel

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.970
Cedric Leighton.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.638
Phil, first to you.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.206
The president did speak

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.041
just before we learned this news

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.376
about these latest attacks,

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.377
about this U.S.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.245
service member

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:06.479
who was injured

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.748
What is President Biden saying about

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.283
what does appear to be

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.151
an escalating tit for tat

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:14.988
You know,

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:15.421
Alex, this

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.256
entire trip, well,

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.457
it certainly has been focused

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.558
on the bilateral relationship

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.292
between the U.S.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.226
and Canada

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.828
has faced the reality

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.329
of this acceleration

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.564
with Iranian proxies

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.598
since the very start.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:25.999
The president

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.201
finding out about the initial attack

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.769
that killed American contractor

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.536
and wounded U.S.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.372
servicemen on his way here on Air

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.640
Force One was briefed about

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.574
that was provided

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.642
options by the Pentagon

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:36.542
and made the decision

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.644
to give the green light

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.112
on the retaliatory strikes

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.313
we saw last night,

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.081
all while on his way to Canada.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.216
During that press conference

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:43.716
just a short

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.284
while ago

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.218
was when the reports

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.919
of that second and third attack

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.354
just today came out.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.522
Now, when the president was asked

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.757
about the initial attack,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.624
this was his response

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.294
last night, U.S.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.128
military forces

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:55.595
carried out

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:58.665
a series of airstrikes in Syria targeting

00:04:58.665 --> 00:04:59.632
those responsible

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.168
for attacking our personnel.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.803
My heart and deepest condolences

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.905
go out to the family of the American

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:06.939
we lost

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.341
and wish a speedy recovery

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.809
for those who were wounded.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:10.643
Make no mistake,

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.678
the United States does

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.913
not does not emphasize

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:17.550
seek conflict with Iran, but be prepared

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.553
to first forcefully protect our people.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.924
That's exactly what happened last night.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.894
And it's been notable U.S.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:28.194
officials

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.162
throughout the course of the day

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:29.729
making clear

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.197
they do not want to escalate

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.433
any type of situation or conflict

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:34.667
with Iran directly.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.036
But they will respond if necessary.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.571
The question is what defines

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:39.439
if necessary?

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:41.174
It has certainly been when U.S.

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.542
troops have been attacked, injured

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.643
or killed.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:44.844
We'll have to see whether or not that's

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.346
been the case, the latest attacks

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.547
and whether or not that draws

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:48.815
or drives a response

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:49.849
from President Biden.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.084
Yeah, they don't want to escalate.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:51.784
But Colonel Leighton,

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:52.485
as you just heard

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:53.753
from Oren Liebermann in the Pentagon

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.722
for attacks in the past 24 hours

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:57.490
now, yet another U.S.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:00.059
service member who was who was wounded.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.995
How worried are you about this spiraling

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:05.631
Well, I think,

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.934
Alex, that it's a real risk.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:08.201
You know,

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:10.503
the Iranians have used these proxies

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.372
for quite some time.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.741
And the use of proxies

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:16.442
is a way of allowing the Iranians

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.177
to wash their hands of things.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.913
But it also means that they are not under

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:21.881
direct control

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.716
all the time of the Iranians.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.251
So they could be acting in a way

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.353
that could exacerbate the situation

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:29.222
and create some real problems.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:29.722
And that,

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:30.423
I think, is something

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.158
that we have to be concerned about.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.326
Yeah, that is a very important point.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.560
We don't know about the communication

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.561
between Tehran

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.397
and these Iranian backed proxies.

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.398
Phil, I want to go back to you

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:38.765
and something

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:39.365
you just mentioned,

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.066
the administration

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.401
saying clearly repeatedly

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.869
that they don't want escalation

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:43.536
with Iran.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:44.871
But we have seen Iran

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.606
ramping up this aggression

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.874
as well as its support

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.375
for Russia and their war

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.210
in Ukraine, providing those weapons.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:51.878
So more

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:53.613
generally for this administration,

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.181
how much of a growing threat

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:56.549
is Iran becoming

00:06:59.085 --> 00:06:59.585
You know, Alex,

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:01.020
and you know this area of the world

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:01.721
quite well.

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:02.889
I'm not sure it ever really

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:03.756
left the table

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.291
as a very significant threat,

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.692
even if it hasn't been front of mind,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:07.293
certainly

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.929
since the invasion of Ukraine by Russia.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:10.630
But as you noted,

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.765
the sheer number of drones

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:13.699
and weapons capabilities

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:14.200
that the Iranians

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.234
have been providing to

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.702
the Russians has been noted

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.805
repeatedly by U.S. officials.

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:19.772
Also keep in mind,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:20.606
it was just over the course

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.574
of the last couple of weeks

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.643
that it has become clear and very public

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.311
just how rapidly

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:27.213
Iran has accelerated its ability

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.915
to have that breakout period right now

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:31.217
and how that shifts the context

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.885
or how U.S. officials approach this.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:33.719
They've made very clear

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:35.054
their early stage efforts

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.823
to get back into the Iran nuclear

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.424
deal are no longer an option.

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:39.659
They haven't laid out

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:40.827
what actually comes next,

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:42.328
but it's very clear

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.197
that this is moving back to front of mind

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:45.631
and only seems to be accelerating based

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:45.765
on what

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:47.333
we've seen from their proxies,

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.234
at least over the course

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.535
of the last 48 hours.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:51.070
All right. Very worrying developments.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:51.604
Phil, Colonel

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:53.372
Leighton, I want you to stay with me.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:56.008
I want to bring in CNN's Fareed Zakaria,

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:57.210
the host of Fareed

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.878
Zakaria GPS

00:07:58.878 --> 00:07:59.445
Fareed,

00:07:59.445 --> 00:07:59.946
thanks so much

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:01.247
for joining us this evening.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:03.683
After this latest strike on these U.S.

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:04.684
forces, which again

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:06.719
wounded at least one U.S. service member.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.921
How concerned are you about the

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:10.122
possibility of escalation?

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:13.726
Very concerned, Alex.

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:15.394
Look, the situation is very,

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:16.696
very dangerous,

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:18.598
largely because the United States

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:19.465
and Iran

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:20.833
have the worst relations

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.568
they have had in decades.

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:23.469
And, you know,

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:24.403
that's saying something

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:25.204
because they've never had

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:27.440
particularly good relations

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.975
But let me remind us

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:29.842
all of a little bit

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.377
of historical context.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:34.180
If you go back just six or seven years

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:35.348
and say,

00:08:35.348 --> 00:08:35.815
you know,

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:36.516
the last years

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:38.050
of the Obama administration,

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.619
even the first year of the Trump

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:40.620
administration,

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.588
Iran was actually helping

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:46.058
the United States defeat ISIS in Iraq.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:48.961
Iran was sending its militias to do that.

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:52.198
It was adhering to the nuclear deal.

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:53.866
It was observing the limits.

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:54.800
And the U.S.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.736
was in dialog with

00:08:56.736 --> 00:08:58.471
then Trump pulls out of the deal.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:01.073
Iran now sees itself in a box.

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:04.043
Its economy is squeezed, it is desperate,

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.379
and it is searching for ways

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.481
to, in a sense, show

00:09:08.681 --> 00:09:10.750
that it has some capacity.

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:12.752
And that capacity is largely

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:13.953
for troublemaking.

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:14.921
It is unleashing

00:09:14.921 --> 00:09:16.923
more of these militias over,

00:09:16.923 --> 00:09:18.658
which has even the US government admits

00:09:18.658 --> 00:09:21.027
it doesn't have perfect control.

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:23.763
And it's always played a nasty game

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.398
with militias like Hezbollah

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:27.266
and the ones in Syria.

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:29.702
So the whole situation is one

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:31.137
which Iran doesn't

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:33.573
have a lot to gain from,

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:35.508
from stabilizing the situation.

00:09:35.508 --> 00:09:37.877
The United States, entirely

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.346
justifiably has to respond

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.915
when its forces are threatened.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.383
But you put that all together

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:45.384
and it's a powder keg

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:47.653
How much do you think that

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:49.422
this is going to change U.S.

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:51.857
priorities in the Middle East, Fareed,

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:54.126
especially as China and Russia

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:54.493
try to

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:57.964
expand their influence in the region

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.732
the Middle East has this affect.

00:09:59.732 --> 00:09:59.899
You know,

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:01.634
it's like the line out of Godfather

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:02.735
three where

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:03.903
Michael Corleone says,

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:04.937
I keep trying to get out

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:06.238
of the family business

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:08.441
and you keep pulling me back

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:11.510
the Middle East is like that business.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.712
You know, the U.S.

00:10:12.712 --> 00:10:14.814
gets drawn back in because of things

00:10:14.814 --> 00:10:16.315
like this violence,

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:17.950
violence against American soldiers.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.186
There's instability.

00:10:21.087 --> 00:10:22.021
You can tell that

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:23.823
the Biden administration is trying

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:24.957
to keep this as

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:25.758
as common,

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:26.492
as in control,

00:10:26.492 --> 00:10:28.194
precisely for the reason

00:10:28.194 --> 00:10:29.729
you were outlining it.

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.230
The Biden administration believes

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.531
it has bigger fish to fry.

00:10:32.531 --> 00:10:35.134
And strategically, that's exactly right.

00:10:35.134 --> 00:10:37.069
But there is a reality,

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:38.838
a tactic makes things implode.

00:10:38.838 --> 00:10:40.139
If there is the optics

00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:42.074
of American soldiers under fire.

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:42.541
The Biden

00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:44.176
people will have to do something.

00:10:44.176 --> 00:10:44.977
But so far,

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:46.278
I think they're trying their

00:10:46.278 --> 00:10:48.114
best to maintain that focus.

